  "notes": "Cash-basis school district; all funds governmental (School Nutrition and Activities are governmental funds here), so business_type is null. Receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column (trimmed pp4-5). Beginning 7,912,562 and ending 9,700,778 are the printed fund balances (p5). Printed total receipts 13,814,355 is 1 more than the lines add to (13,814,354); roll-forward ties with the lines. Transfers: General in 11,607 (from Cooperative), out 100,000 (School Nutrition 80,000 + Activities 20,000); cross-check ties. Activities Fund schedule prints 282,289 receipts which includes the 20,000 transfer; split using statement. General Fund schedule (pp7-10) is more detailed than the statement; the Depreciation Fund is combined into the General Fund column of the statement (statement GF beginning 6,860,874 = 5,099,540 + 1,761,334); it has its own detail schedule (p11). General Fund state sources lines add to 2,861,292 versus printed total 4,955,347 (see report_discrepancies). Detail budget-only lines with no actual (6310, 6421-6423, 6990, 6992, depreciation 'Other local receipts', coop local receipts) omitted. Detail 'budget_final' on Activities receipts is the budget for the combined line. Public power district sales tax classed as other taxes. State/federal program disbursements classed as instruction (review). Balance sheet from the cash-basis net position statement (p3); no liabilities. Read pages 1-16 of 16 Recheck: 'County sources' 84,323 recategorized to fines and forfeitures (83,050 is 2110 County fines and license fees, p7), detail 2110 likewise. Cooperative Fund schedule (p15) prints no total line, only the Transfers 11,607 disbursement (recorded as other financing), so it has no detail_totals entry."
}